For installation instructions from a diskette, please see INSTALL.DOC.

If you are downloading these demonstration files, the files you should
be downloading are:

  IDCD1.ZIP -- TCXL-DOS, TCXL/Graphics and TCXL/Windows demo programs
  IDCD2.ZIP -- TCXL-DOS and TCXL/Windows TesSeRact User Interface demos
  IDCD3.ZIP -- TCXL/Editor and TesSeRact File Management System demos
  IDCD4.ZIP -- TCXL Advanced Utilities, TesSeRact Compression System
                 and TesSeRact Printer Control System demos
  IDCD5.ZIP -- TCXL Demonstration "shell" programs for TCXL-DOS and
                 TCXL/Windows (TCXLDEMO.EXE and TCXLDEMW.EXE)


After downloading these files, create a new directory called "TCXL60D", 
copy the files into this directory, and run:

  PKUNZIP IDCD?.ZIP

This will extract the files from all the ZIPs you are installing.  In all
cases except IDCD5.ZIP (which just contains the demo shell programs), you
will have an executable file with the same name as the ZIP -- IDCD1.EXE,
etc.  Execute these files in any order to create the appropriate demo
files.

----------------------------------

After installation, you should have the following files:

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TCXLDEMO.EXE
TCXLDEMW.EXE
TCXLDEMO.IDC
TCXLDEMW.IDC
DEMO\TCXLDEMO.H

TCXLDEMO is the DOS version of a shell program that runs various individual
demo programs, listed in a menu.  Only those demos that are actually present
on your installation will be selectable.  TCXLDEMO was built with the TCXL-DOS
library, and uses TSpawn() (one of IDC's Advanced Utilities) to swap itself out
of memory when executing programs.  TCXLDEMW is the Windows version of
TCXLDEMO, and was built using TCXL/Windows, using the same source code as the
DOS version.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
ALLTCXLD.EXE
ALLTCXLG.EXE
ALLTCXLW.EXE
DEMO\ALLMISC.C
DEMO\ALLTCXL.C
DEMO\ALLTCXL.H
ALLTUID.EXE
ALLTUIW.EXE
DEMO\ALLTUI.C

ALLTCXL is a program that demonstrates many of TCXL's capabilities, including
menus, entry forms, online help, and scrolling virtual windows.  The File
pulldown menu includes a functional scrolling file viewer, an order-entry form
with printing capability, and a directory listing function.  Online context-
sensitive help can be invoked at any time by pressing F1.  All menu items can
be selected either from the keyboard or with the mouse.  ALLTCXL is provided
in three version: ALLTCXLD.EXE (DOS text), ALLTCXLG.EXE (DOS graphics), and
ALLTCXLW.EXE (Windows).  All three versions were built from the same source
code.

ALLTUI is equivalent to the ALLTCXL demo program, but is implemented using
TCXL's new TesSeRact User Interface, or TUI.  TUI is a portable, CUA-style
interface that is much easier to use than typical event-driven systems.  A
TUI program compiled with TCXL/Windows is a true Windows application, with
all the standard controls and capabilities.  The same program built with
TCXL-DOS gives you a Windows-style interface under DOS.  ALLTUI is provides
in a Windows version (ALLTUIW.EXE) and a DOS version (ALLTUID.EXE), both
built from the same source code.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TPRNDEMO.EXE
DEMO\TPRNDEMO.C
DRIVER\DEFAULT.PRT
DRIVER\DESKINT.PRT
DRIVER\DESKPLUS.PRT
DRIVER\DIABLO.PRT
DRIVER\DOSTEXT.PRT
DRIVER\EPSON.PRT
DRIVER\HOUSTON.PRT
DRIVER\HPLJSII.PRT
DRIVER\HPPLOT.PRT
DRIVER\IBMCOMP.PRT
DRIVER\IBMGRAPH.PRT
DRIVER\IBMPRO.PRT
DRIVER\IBMPROPR.PRT
DRIVER\IBMQUIET.PRT
DRIVER\NECSPIN.PRT
DRIVER\OKIDATA.PRT
DRIVER\PANASON.PRT
DRIVER\PANASON9.PRT
DRIVER\TOSHIBA.PRT

TPRNDEMO demonstrates TPRINT, the TesSeRact Printer Control System.  It will
print to the printer port of your choice (or to a file) using the printer
driver that you select.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
EDTDEMO.EXE
DEMO\EDTDEMO.C

EDTDEMO is a functional full-screen editor built using TCXL/Editor (TEDT).
EDTDEMO will edit any text file that you specify on the command line.  If
no file is specified, it will display its own source code.  EDTDEMO makes
full use of TEDT's ability to hook into TCXL's menu and help systems.  You
can use EDTDEMO to try TEDT's scrolling, cursor movement, block manipulation,
and searching capabilities, as well as all other standard text-editing
activities.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TFILDEMO.EXE
DEMO\TFILDEMO.C
DEMO\TFILDEMO.H
MAIL.DBF
MAIL.DBT
MAIL.NDX
MAIL.NTX

TFILDEMO demonstrates TFILE, the TesSeRact File Management System.  TFILDEMO
allows you to view and edit an indexed database file in DBF format.  The
browser interface was implemented using a TCXL entry form.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
ADVDEMO.EXE
DEMO\ADVDEMO.C
DEMO\ADVDEMO.H

ADVDEMO demonstrates some of the products that are included in the TCXL
Advanced Utilities.  TSpawn() is used to execute an external program while
swapping the current application out of active memory.  TRedir() gives a
TCXL program the ability to redirect the screen output of any DOS program
into a TCXL window.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TCMPDEMO.EXE
DEMO\TCMPDEMO.C
DEMO\TCMPDEMO.H

TCMPDEMO demonstrates the TesSeRact Compression System.  You can use any of
the various compression methods provided with TCOMP, and compare the results,
using any file you select.
